\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19.1.1}{\ignorespaces The \(\min \)-segment tree on CSES~1649's own array \((3,2,4,5,1,1,5,3)\) (leaves \(t_{8..15}\), heap layout). Each internal node is the minimum of its green interval: \(t_4{=}\min (3,2){=}2\), \(t_6{=}\min (1,1){=}1\), \(t_2{=}\min (t_4,t_5){=}\min (2,4){=}2\) (the answer to query \texttt  {2 1 4}), \(t_3{=}\min (t_6,t_7){=}1\) (answer to \texttt  {2 5 6} after a cover), and the root \(t_1{=}\min (t_2,t_3){=}1\). This eight-leaf tree is the top of the opener's sixteen-leaf \(A\)-tree -- same rule, one level shorter.}}{1154}{figure.caption.203}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c13-minbuild}{{19.1.1}{1154}{The \(\min \)-segment tree on CSES~1649's own array \((3,2,4,5,1,1,5,3)\) (leaves \(t_{8..15}\), heap layout). Each internal node is the minimum of its green interval: \(t_4{=}\min (3,2){=}2\), \(t_6{=}\min (1,1){=}1\), \(t_2{=}\min (t_4,t_5){=}\min (2,4){=}2\) (the answer to query \texttt {2 1 4}), \(t_3{=}\min (t_6,t_7){=}1\) (answer to \texttt {2 5 6} after a cover), and the root \(t_1{=}\min (t_2,t_3){=}1\). This eight-leaf tree is the top of the opener's sixteen-leaf \(A\)-tree -- same rule, one level shorter}{figure.caption.203}{}}
