\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19.4.1}{\ignorespaces The \(2n\) array-resident tree over the same \(n{=}8\) min-instance \((3,2,4,5,1,1,5,3)\) as \(Figure~\ref {fig:c13-minbuild}\). Leaves occupy the back half \(t[8..15]\); the front half \(t[1..7]\) is filled by \(Code~\ref {lst:c13-iter}\)'s second loop, \(t_i=\min (t_{2i},t_{2i+1})\), from \(i{=}7\) down to \(1\). The values are \emph  {identical} to the recursive \(4n\) tree because \(n{=}8\) is a power of two -- only the walk changes, and no slots are wasted.}}{1180}{figure.caption.209}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c13-iter2n}{{19.4.1}{1180}{The \(2n\) array-resident tree over the same \(n{=}8\) min-instance \((3,2,4,5,1,1,5,3)\) as \(\figref {c13-minbuild}\). Leaves occupy the back half \(t[8..15]\); the front half \(t[1..7]\) is filled by \(\coderef {c13-iter}\)'s second loop, \(t_i=\min (t_{2i},t_{2i+1})\), from \(i{=}7\) down to \(1\). The values are \emph {identical} to the recursive \(4n\) tree because \(n{=}8\) is a power of two -- only the walk changes, and no slots are wasted}{figure.caption.209}{}}
